STEP 1: TEST DESIGN GENERATION (FROM SPECIFICATION ONLY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Pair Input - Prompt A to Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B]:
"You are designing automated specification-based tests for the Other Academic Procedures (OAP) Fusion ERP module.
Source of truth: Use ONLY the supplied Problem Statement and Use Case Specifications below.
Do NOT inspect implementation code.
Do NOT infer behavior from implementation.
Do NOT introduce behavior unsupported by the supplied specification.
Generate the minimum non-redundant set of test cases needed to satisfy the strategy-specific adequacy rule in Section 7.
For every test case output exactly these fields: test_id, source_id, purpose, preconditions, action_or_input, expected_result, test_type.
Output ONLY a valid JSON array.

Strategy-specific instruction for UC:
Cover the main success flow of every Use Case and every explicitly specified alternative/exception flow with at least one test. Do not invent additional flows."

[Model Output Summary]:
The model returned a comprehensive JSON array containing 53 test cases covering
all 25 OAP Use Cases (OA-UC-01 through OA-UC-92).

[Pair Verification & Freezing]:
We validated that each Use Case has its main success scenario tested as well as
stated alternate flows (e.g., student cancellations, rejection workflows, re-submissions).
Test IDs TC-UC-001 through TC-UC-053 were verified. The JSON was saved and permanently
frozen to: `a8_design/UC_DESIGN.json`.

